messages.reasoning_content:
The detailed description reveals the exact cause of the `CreateContainerConfigError`.

The event message states:
`Warning Failed 5s (x7 over 64s) kubelet spec.containers{app}: Error: container has runAsNonRoot and image will run as root (pod: "app-5dcbf687b-nvchz_restricted-app(3325329e-2d8a-4c82-8d16-4eb612b66088)", container: app)`

This is a conflict between the security context I applied (`runAsNonRoot: true`) and the base image (`busybox:1.37.0`), which does not allow running as a non-root user by default when using the command specified (`sh -c exec sleep 3600`). The image needs to be configured or replaced to support running as a non-root user while maintaining the desired security posture.

Since I cannot change the image to one guaranteed to run as non-root without more context, and the constraint is to make the workload run while keeping security settings, the most direct fix is to modify the deployment to specify a `runAsUser` within the security context, forcing it to a non-root UID, which is the standard way to resolve this conflict when using base images that lack a default non-root entrypoint.

I must patch the Deployment again to add `runAsUser` to the security context. A common non-root UID is 1000.

New patch payload will add `runAsUser: 1000` to the existing security context. I'll use a strategic merge patch to update the existing structure.

Original patch was:
```json
[
  {
    "op": "add",
    "path": "/spec/template/spec/containers/0/securityContext",
    "value": {
      "allowPrivilegeEscalation": false,
      "capabilities": {
        "drop": [
          "ALL"
        ]
      },
      "runAsNonRoot": true,
      "seccompProfile": {
        "type": "RuntimeDefault"
      }
    }
  }
]
```
I will update this patch to include `runAsUser: 1000`. Since `kubectl patch --type json` replaces the value at the path, I need to redefine the entire securityContext object, adding the new field.

Revised security context:
```json
{
  "allowPrivilegeEscalation": false,
  "capabilities": {
    "drop": [
      "ALL"
    ]
  },
  "runAsNonRoot": true,
  "runAsUser": 1000,
  "seccompProfile": {
    "type": "RuntimeDefault"
  }
}
```

I will apply this revised patch to the existing deployment.

